FORMAT: 1A
HOST: https://live.fleetr.com/api/v1

# Fleet Management API
This is an API built using **API Blueprint** to demonstrate managing fleet operations, dispatch and maintenance hosted on [Fleet.com API](http://developers.fleetr.com/reference).

NOTE: This document is a **work in progress**.

## Group Users
Resources related to fleet operation management.

### Fleet Operation Workflows [/fleet]

#### List All Vehicles [GET /fleet/vehicles{?limit,page,status,type}]
Retrieve a paginated list of registered vehicles.

+ Parameters
    + limit: 10 (number, optional) - The maximum number of users to return.
    + page: 1 (number, optional) - The page number to fetch.
    + status: "available", "occupied" (enum, optional) - The status of the vehicle
    + type: "tricycle", "van" (enum, optional) - The type of the vehicle

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Attributes (array[Vehicle])

#### Register a Vehicle [POST /fleet/vehicles]
Register a new vehicle in the system.

+ Request (application/json)
    + Attributes
        + vin: `1N084995TNE986SIZN49930` (string, required) - Vehicle Identification Number.
        + licence_plate_number: `ABC-234-TY` (string, required) - Plate Number.

+ Response 211 (application/json)
    + Attributes (Vehicle)

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    + Header
        Retry-After: 230
    + Body
        {
            "error": "Email address already registered."
        }


## Group Dsipatches
Resources related to managing dispatches.

### Dispatch Operations Workflow [POST /dispatch/trips]

+ Parameters
    + dispatch_request_id: `12345` (string, required) - The unique identifier of the task.

#### View Task Details [GET]
Returns detailed information about a specific task.

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Attributes (Trip)

+ Response 404 (application/json)
    + Headers
        Set-Cookie: last_request_status=error_transient; HttpOnly; Path=/; Secure; SameSite=Lax; Expires=
        Vary: User-Agent, Accept
    + Body
        {
            "error": "Task not found."
        }

#### Update Task [PUT]
Modify the status or details of an existing task.

+ Request (application/json)
    + Attributes
        + title: `Buy groceries` (string, optional)
        + is_completed: true (boolean, required)

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Attributes (Task)

#### Delete Task [DELETE]
Permanently remove a task from the system.

+ Response 204


### Data Structures

### Vehicle (object)
+ id: `usr_987` (string, required) - Unique identifier for the user.
+ vin: `Jane Doe` (string, required) - The user's name.
+ license_plate_number: `jane.doe@example.com` (string, required)

### Trip (object)
+ dispatch_request_id: `tsk_123` (string, required) - Unique identifier for the task.
+ assignment_id: `Finish documentation` (string, required) - Title of the task.
+ status: false (boolean, required) - Completion state.
